Doenet-Sync-Version: 0.7.28
Doenet-Sync-NumVariants: 1
Doenet-Sync-Hash: d4d2efad7cf28b11
-->
<problem>
<!-- <title>analytic stability of ODE equilibria, dx/dt=quadratic*e^x, quadratic two zeros</title> -->

<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="a" from="-4" to=" 4" exclude="0" />
<selectFromSequence name="b" from="-10" to=" 10" exclude="0" numToSelect="2" withReplacement="false" />
<selectFromSequence name="x0" from="-10" to=" 10" />


<select name="x">x y z u v w p X Y Z S</select>
<function name="quadratic" variables="$x" symbolic="true"><math expand="true" simplify="true">$a*($x -$b[1] )*($x -$b[2] )</math></function>

<function name="fun" variables="$x" symbolic="true"><math simplify="numbers">$$quadratic($x)*e^$x</math></function>

<mathList name="Es">
  <sort name="E1">$b[1] $b[2]</sort>
</mathList>

<derivative name="fprime" variables="$x">$fun</derivative>
<function name="fprime_factor" variables="$x"><math simplify="true">($$quadratic($x )+<derivative variables="$x">$$quadratic($x)</derivative>)*e^$x </math></function>

<evaluate name="fprime_E1" forceNumeric="true" function="$fprime" input="$E1[1]" displayDigits="5" />
<evaluate name="fprime_E2" forceNumeric="true" function="$fprime" input="$E1[2]" displayDigits="5" />

<boolean name="E1_stable">$fprime_E1  &lt; 0</boolean>
<boolean name="E2_stable">$fprime_E2  &lt; 0</boolean>

<conditionalContent name="E1_stability">
  <case condition="$E1_stable"><text>stable</text></case>
  <else><text>unstable</text></else>
</conditionalContent>

<conditionalContent name="E2_stability">
  <case condition="$E2_stable"><text>stable</text></case>
  <else><text>unstable</text></else>
</conditionalContent>
 
<math name="fun_expand" expand="true" simplify="true">$fun</math>

</setup>



<p>Consider the 
  <select>
    <option>differential equation</option>
    <option>dynamical system</option>
  </select>
<md>
  <mrow>
   <select name="derivString">
     <option>\frac{ d$x }{ dt }</option>
     <option>$x'(t)</option>
   </select>
  \amp = <math extend="$fun.formula" /></mrow>
  <mrow>$x _0\amp = $x0 </mrow>
  <mrow />
</md>
</p>
<p>
Find all the equilibria and determine their stability.
</p>


<p>Number of equilibria: <mathInput name="n_e" /></p>

<p>The equilibria are</p>
<ul>
  <repeatForSequence length="min(5, $n_e)" name="mapEs"><li><m>$(x)_e = </m> <mathInput /></li></repeatForSequence>
</ul>
<answer>
<award matchPartial="true">
  <when unorderedCompare="true">
    <mathList><setup><collect isResponse="true" componentType="mathInput" from="$mapEs" name="collect_collectedEs" /></setup><mathList name="collectedEs" extend="$collect_collectedEs.value" /></mathList>
    = $Es
  </when>
</award>
</answer>

<p>Stability of equilibria:</p>
<ul>
  <repeat for="$collectedEs" name="mapStab" valueName="v">
      <li><m>$(x)_e = $v</m>:
      <choiceInput inline="true">
        <choice>stable</choice>
        <choice>unstable</choice>
      </choiceInput>
      </li>
    </repeat>
</ul>
  
<answer maxNumAttempts="3">
  <award matchPartial="true" matchByExactPositions="true">
    <when>
      <textList><setup><collect componentType="choiceInput" from="$mapStab" isResponse="true" name="collect_list" /></setup><textList name="list" extend="$collect_list.selectedValue" /></textList>
      =
      <textList>
        <repeatForSequence length="2" indexName="i">
            <conditionalContent>
              <case condition="$collectedEs[$i] = $E1[1]">
                <text>$E1_stability[1][1]</text>
              </case>
              <case condition="$collectedEs[$i] = $E1[2]">
                <text>$E2_stability[1][1]</text>
              </case>
              <else><text>invalid</text></else>
            </conditionalContent>
          </repeatForSequence>
      </textList>
    </when>
  </award>
</answer>



<solution>
<p>To find equilibria, set <m>$derivString = 0</m>.  If we let <m>f($x ) =<math extend="$fun.formula" /></m>, then an equilibrium <m>$x _e</m> must satisfy <m>f($x _e)=0</m>, or
<me>$$fun($(x)_e) =0.</me>
Since the exponential cannot be zero, the only possibility is that <m>$quadratic =0</m>.  
We can solve this equation by factoring or using the quadratic formula.  The result is that <m>$x _e = $b[1] </m> or <m>$x _e=$b[2] </m>.</p>

<p>To determine stability, we need to evaluate the derivative <m>f'($x )</m>.  Using the product rule, the derivative is 
<md>
  <mrow>f'($x )\amp = <math extend="$fprime.formula" /></mrow>
  <mrow>\amp = <math extend="$fprime_factor.formula" /></mrow>
</md>
 We evaluate the derivative at each of the equilibria.</p>


<p>To determine the stability of <m>$x _e = $E1[1] </m>, we calculate that <m>f'($E1[1] ) = $fprime_E1
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$E1_stable">
 \lt 
</case>
<else>
 \gt 
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 0</m>.  Therefore <m>$x _e=$E1[1] </m> is $E1_stability[1][1] .</p>

<p>To determine the stability of <m>$x _e = $E1[2] </m>, we calculate that <m>f'($E1[2] ) = $fprime_E2 
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$E2_stable">
 \lt 
</case>
<else>
 \gt 
</else>
</conditionalContent>
 0</m>.  Therefore <m>$x _e=$E1[2] </m> is $E2_stability[1][1] .</p>

</solution>


</problem>